    "pk": 2,
    "fields": {
        "car_title": "2017 Ford Edge",
        "state": "TX",
        "city": "Dallas",
        "color": "Black",
        "model": "Edge",
        "year": 2017,
        "condition": "Used",
        "price": "25000.00",
        "description": "<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Ford Edge</strong>&nbsp;is a&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crossover_(automobile)\" title=\"Crossover (automobile)\">crossover SUV</a>&nbsp;manufactured and marketed by the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Motor_Company\" title=\"Ford Motor Company\">Ford Motor Company</a>&nbsp;introduced for the 2007 model year as the first&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mid-size_CUV\" title=\"Mid-size CUV\">mid-size CUV</a>&nbsp;marketed by Ford in North America. Deriving its name from a trim package of the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Ranger_(Americas)\" title=\"Ford Ranger (Americas)\">Ford Ranger</a>, the Ford Edge is positioned between the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Escape\" title=\"Ford Escape\">Ford Escape</a>&nbsp;and the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Explorer\" title=\"Ford Explorer\">Ford Explorer</a>&nbsp;within the Ford product line.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Production of the North American Edge ended in April 2024,<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Edge#cite_note-3\">[3]</a>&nbsp;with the third generation Edge (dubbed the Edge L), launched in 2023, being produced and sold exclusively in China.</p>",
